From c168ccaa52a2066ecb35db20ef21093a3ee257b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:45:19 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A missile's look can set its speed (SetMissileLook's tenth
 number), and the twenty-third round

`SetMissileLook(spellId, colour, width, seconds, scale, spin, caster, axis, speed)`: a last number
flies the dressed missile at that many yards a second from where it is, over the speed its spell
gives it and over the 100 yd/s cap the launch's refit keeps (up to 400 now), so a hurled weapon can
cross the field as fast as a thrown axe should. `0` or nothing keeps the spell's own, and every
older line (nine arguments) reads as before. `HasActionCombat()` says 23, and the module's notes
list this round's additions: the lower-body clip (0037), the crossfade between clips (0038), the
glowing object (0039) and this.
